WEBVTT

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.000
Sakamoto-san?

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.590
<i>Reppuzan!</i>

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.020
Incredible.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:25.950
Miyafuji?

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:29.120
Y-Your Reppuzan is
such a powerful attack.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.290
It's weak.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.670
I'm trying to learn a Reppuzan that'll top Reppuzan...

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:36.920
The "True Reppuzan."

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.340
True Reppuzan?

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:43.930
Yes. It's a secret technique passed down
in the Fuso Empire since time immemorial.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.060
If I'm able to master it,

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:49.140
I'll be able to obliterate even the strongest Neuroi in one strike.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:54.520
Sakamoto-san! Please teach me the Reppuzan, too!

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.110
I want to destroy Neuroi and bring
peace to the world as quickly as possible.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:02:59.820
That's impossible.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.320
A rookie like you could
never use such an attack.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.200
I'll try my best!

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.450
So please, teach it to me!

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.000
No.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.970
Oh, Miyafuji. You're late.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:27.270
Tonight is zuppa di farro
and vongole bianco!

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.060
We made it.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.600
Okay.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.100
Huh?

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.440
What's wrong, Yoshika-chan?

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.230
Are you not feeling well?

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:41.110
Oh, not at all. I feel great.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.200
Then eat!

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:44.620
Even if you're not hungry.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.330
You think someone who
doesn't fuel themselves

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.580
will be 100% ready to fight in an emergency?

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.710
U-Understood...

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.620
Fuel?

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:57.840
Geez... I don't wanna hear army lectures every waking moment.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:59.590
Hey, Hartmann!

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.130
Is that how a Karlsland
soldier should speak?

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.510
There she goes again.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:08.260
Listen to me. Unlike the situation in Britannia, we're heavily lacking in firepower.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.770
Our role has never been more critical.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:14.190
<i>She's right. I need to work harder.</i>

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:18.570
<i>Sakamoto-san probably won't teach it to me because she thinks I'm not dependable.</i>

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:19.780
All right.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.530
Thanks for the meal!

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.750
<i>She's fast... Faster than before.</i>

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.670
<i>But not faster than me!</i>

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:45.550
I've got you!

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:48.600
She rolled left?

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:49.430
Now!

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.270
Not so fast.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.100
<i>She missed from such close range?</i>

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.400
Huh? What?

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:00.820
You're mine.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.320
The match is over.
Perrine-san is the winner.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.620
B-But of course. She never stood a chance.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.540
<i>That's strange. It's like, all of a sudden, I lost power.</i>

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.170
Miyafuji-san?

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.000
Ah... Yes!

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.590
What're you just hovering there for?

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.460
We have two more rounds!

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.600
The match is over.
Perrine-san is the winner.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.850
<i>What's going on? I'm having trouble flying.</i>

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.770
It's not like her to lose
three matches in a row.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.110
Miyafuji-san, don't hold back just because this is training.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.780
Or am I took weak for you to go 100%?

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.950
It's not that! I'm not holding back.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.750
I see. So you noticed it, too, Perrine.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:06.010
Yes. Something was strange in the way she was moving today.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:08.130
She wasn't her usual self.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:09.930
All right.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:11.930
Thank you for bringing
this to my attention.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.560
You're very considerate, Perrine.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:14.470
Huh?

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:15.810
Oh, no...

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:21.690
I just figured we must take every
precaution to maximize our combat abilities.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:24.360
It's not that I was concerned about Miyafuji-san.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:32.030
We crosschecked everything,
but didn't notice anything unusual.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.580
The magic engine has been given a complete overhaul.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:39.920
I swapped in some new plugs and oil, just to be safe, but...

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:43.040
I see. So nothing's wrong with the Striker.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:45.130
Understood. Thank you.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:49.970
<i>Then that means the problem is with Miyafuji herself.</i>

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.220
Done. You can put your
clothes back on now.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:55.810
Okay.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.020
She gets a clean bill of health from me.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:00.650
I see.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:04.190
Why did you want me to undergo a physical, all of a sudden?

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.270
No reason.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:09.900
It's our responsibility, as your superiors,
to check on our troops' health from time to time.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.030
But you said there's nothing wrong with me, right?

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:15.330
That's correct. You're in excellent health.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.240
We should all be so lucky.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:22.670
Actually, the one thing I'm really proud of is that I've never even had a cold.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.750
Hey. What are you two doing there?

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:28.840
S-Sorry...

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:32.130
Oh, Lynne-chan, Perrine-san!

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:34.680
Is something wrong with you, Yoshika-chan?

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:38.770
Nope. It was just a physical. I'm totally fine.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.520
Oh, thank god!

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:45.270
My goodness. It's very important for Witches to take care of themselves!

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:47.730
Like I said, I'm totally fine.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:50.650
But that makes it all the more odd.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.950
Barkhorn... When did you get here?

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.950
I verified that you're having trouble flying.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:59.950
Until we get to the root of the problem, I cannot send you into battle.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.170
Is that true, Yoshika-chan?
You're having problems flying?

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:07.290
I'm ordering you grounded on base, until we know what's disabling you.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.130
No! I swear I can fly!

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.050
That was an order from a superior officer.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.220
Order...

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:16.010
Yeah. I think it's for the best.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:17.260
No way!

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.140
Yoshika-chan...

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.070
Who's that?

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.070
That's Yoshika.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:36.160
Miyafuji?

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:37.450
What're you doing here?

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:38.530
Huh?

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:39.830
Ah!

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.370
Oh, training on a broom?

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:47.460
Actually, an old lady in my
neighborhood flew on a broom, too.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.500
But why are you training so late at night?

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:55.930
Hey, has either of you ever
become suddenly unable to fly?

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.470
You're not able to fly, Yoshika-chan?

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.510
Huh? Is that true, Miyafuji?

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:03.430
Oh, no. I can still fly...

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.900
Geez. Don't scare me like that.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:07.730
Who is it?

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:11.440
Ouch...

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.610
Hey! What do you think you're doing?!

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.360
Perrine-san!

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:20.240
I-I'm not doing anything...
Just going to the bathroom.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:21.660
You have a bump on your head.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:22.540
What?

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.000
This is all your fault!

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:30.290
All right. All better now.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:33.050
Your magic power seems to be fine.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.880
Isn't that great, Miyafuji?

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:38.010
Hey, now! Would you all stop
treating my head like it's a lab rat?!

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:41.350
Why can't I fly, then?

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:44.180
It's probably best if you rest a bit.

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:47.850
Yeah. I bet you've worked your body too hard lately.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:50.060
I bet everything will be fine,
once you get a good night's sleep.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.150
Just go to bed.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.610
O-Okay.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.830
Fly!

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:21.220
This can't be...

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:24.560
Why... Why can't I fly?

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:27.770
I can't protect anyone like this...

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.520
Lynne-chan...

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.620
Looks like you broke the broom.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:49.580
Isn't the Adriatic beautiful?

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:54.590
We looked out at the sea
like this once before.

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:55.750
Do you remember?

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:57.210
Yeah.

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:02.050
Want me to help you fix the broom?

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:04.600
Yeah. I'd appreciate that.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:23.370
Central command dispatched a radio message

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.200
that in order to strengthen our Romagnan presence,

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:30.210
the Fuso fleet and its flagship,
the battleship Yamato, will arrive tomorrow.

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.790
So it's finally coming here.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.460
Huh? The Yamato?

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.040
You know it, Yoshika-chan?

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.920
Yeah. I saw it when it was docked in Fuso.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.840
It's huge!

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.180
Oh...

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.350
Yes?

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.060
What? The Yamato was in an accident?!

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:48.770
What?!

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:51.690
An accident...

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:53.690
All right. Understood.

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:56.070
That was an emergency request.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:59.440
Earlier, there was an explosion in the Yamato's sickbay.

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:01.320
Quite a few people were injured in the blast.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:04.070
They want us to dispatch
a medic immediately.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:06.530
All right. Ready the type-2 large flying boat.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.830
Please let me go!

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:10.040
I might not be able to fight,

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.750
but I can heal and fly!

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.250
I'm going, too!

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.750
I can put bandages on people.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:16.460
You two...

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.500
I knew they'd say that.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:22.720
They would arrive much
earlier than the flying boat.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:24.640
All right.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:28.560
Miyafuji-san, Lynne-san,
head to the Yamato at once.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:29.810
Roger!

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:36.150
Are you all right, Yoshika-chan?

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.480
Y-Yeah...

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:42.360
<i>What should I do? I'm having trouble flying.</i>

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.280
<i>It's getting worse.</i>

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:46.570
The Yamato!

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:48.620
It's so big!

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:06.430
Are you Miyafuji-san and Lynne-san?

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:08.390
Yes.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.430
This man sustained the worst injuries.

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:13.430
With the equipment here,
we can't do anything more for him.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:16.270
Such horrible injuries...

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.060
Understood.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.650
The bleeding stopped!

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:26.070
Okay. Bandage him up, Lynne-chan.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:26.910
Okay!

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:27.780
Who's next?

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:39.790
<i>Amazing... So this is Miyafuji-san's healing power, which everyone talks about...</i>

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:44.420
Are you all right, Yoshika-chan?
You've healed more than ten people.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:48.430
Yeah, I'm totally fine.
I can keep going for a while.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:50.140
All right. He should be healed now.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:51.720
Where's the next person?

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.520
There isn't one. This is the last casualty.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:55.390
The last one...

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:59.770
Yes. Thanks to your help,
everyone is going to be okay.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.730
I cannot thank you enough.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.940
Isn't that great, Yoshika-chan?

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:05.820
Yeah!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.820
I see. So they're all recovering.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:12.950
After an accident of that proportion, it's a downright miracle.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.540
Miyafuji-san saved us again.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:19.080
How shall we thank her this time?

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:24.880
We sent her a Fuso army doll last time.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.720
It's a report from the radio room!

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:32.930
A Neuroi has been detected at 340 degrees, 60 000 units out!

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:36.430
That's impossible. These are supposed to be safe waters.

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:37.270
Captain.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:40.310
All ships, prepare for battle!

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:43.690
A Neuroi?

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:44.980
Let's go, Lynne-chan.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:45.780
Okay.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:57.370
Neuroi spotted.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:58.580
Where is it?

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:02.210
Grid D-15. Moving at 165 degrees.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:03.840
Hold on... That puts it in the vicinity of...

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:05.750
The Yamato!

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:06.760
That can't be!

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:10.510
They're more than 500 km offshore from Venezia, the location of the Neuroi den.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:13.800
Yeah. They've never strayed
that far away before.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:16.180
But they have.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:18.850
Look, they're heading
toward the Fuso fleet.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:20.140
Damn it.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:42.370
All ships, prepare for anti-air assault.

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.040
Ready main cannons!

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.460
Cannons readied!

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:49.380
Aiming seventy degrees right, 3-0-0!

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.970
Take her starboard!

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:53.340
Starboard ho!

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:58.220
God damn Neuroi...

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:01.520
You're about to find out what the Yamato's forty-six centimeter cannons taste like.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:04.020
Distance, 2-5-0!

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:05.560
Ready to fire!

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.320
Commence attack!

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:14.700
Did you see that? That's the Yamato's power.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.200
Ready the next round!

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:19.790
Are you okay, Lynne-chan?

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.500
Yeah. What was the sound?

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.670
It was so loud... Can you stand?

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:25.670
Yeah.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:26.540
Let's go!

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:27.500
Okay!

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:30.840
Up two! Right two!

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.050
Load heavy artillery!

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.050
Damn... What incredible force...

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:42.390
A direct hit!

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:44.600
Did we get it?

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:50.940
The Takao was hit.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.450
Damn it... They regenerate too fast for us.

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:03.620
Huh?

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:11.210
Why? Why won't they fly?

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:15.180
Yoshika-chan?

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:17.090
H-Hold on a second.

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:27.980
<i>Please... Fly!</i>

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.730
Cruiser Takao, badly damaged!

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:39.120
Yoshika-chan, I'm going in first.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:40.490
Huh?

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:41.580
Lynne-chan!

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.410
Wait! I said, wait!

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:47.540
Lynne-chan!

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:52.250
This is bad. The Takao's been rendered immobile.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.720
It's a sitting duck out there.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.550
Damn. They're going to sink it!

00:17:58.340 --> 00:17:59.430
Lynette-san!

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:00.970
Can you all hear me?

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:04.930
Retreat while I block their attack!

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.810
What are you saying, Lynne-chan?

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.270
I can only buy you a little time!

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:11.940
Hurry and retreat!

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.360
Our presence is crucial
to the war effort here.

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:17.030
We cannot afford to lose the Yamato today.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:20.910
All ships, full speed to port!

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.870
All ships, full speed retreat!

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:25.040
Full speed to port!

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.420
Lynne-chan!

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:37.760
Please... Fly!

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:41.510
Please... Let me fly!

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.350
Thank god.

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.400
It's not working!

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:59.320
The fleet has changed direction.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.070
They're heading away from the Neuroi.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:04.450
They were able to retreat? How'd they manage that?

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:07.790
It looks like Lynne-san is shielding them.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:08.750
What?!

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:15.630
Why... Why won't you let me fly?

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:26.310
Yoshika, you have a power that exceeds
that of both your mother and grandmother.

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:30.690
Grow up, and use your power to protect others from harm.

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:33.560
Okay! I promise!

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:41.030
I'm sorry, Father... I can't keep my promise.

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:42.950
I can't fly anymore!

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:45.780
I can't protect anyone anymore!

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:47.950
Lynne-chan...

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:55.290
Don't cry, Yoshika.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.340
You haven't lost the ability to fly.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:58.510
Huh?

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:02.590
These will be your new wings.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:19.650
A Striker Unit?

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.990
Distance from Neuroi, about three leagues.

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:24.360
We're out of their strike range.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:25.950
I see.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:32.160
Even if we defended the Yamato, we left a Witch alone on the front line.

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:36.790
As a soldier of the Fuso Imperial Military, I feel deeply ashamed.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:40.130
Captain, one of the aft hangars is open.

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:41.130
What?

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.140
<i>Hold on, Lynne-chan.</i>

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:49.310
<i>I'm on my way!</i>

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:51.730
Ah, that's the prototype...

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:53.730
Miyafuji-san, that's too dangerous!

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:56.310
It's never even been on a test flight!

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:03.400
Launch!

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:15.830
Lynne-chan...

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:27.590
<i>I wonder if Yoshika-chan and
the navy men escaped safely...</i>

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:35.980
My shield is weakening...

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:43.690
<i>Yoshika-chan...</i>

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:51.410
Lynne-chan!

00:21:57.420 --> 00:21:59.330
Y-Yoshika-chan...

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:01.630
I'm so sorry I took so long, Lynne-chan.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:03.670
Are you okay? Can you fly?

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:04.670
Yeah.

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:09.760
How dare you... How dare
you attack Lynne-chan!

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:36.960
Yoshika-chan!

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:39.540
Lynne-chan.

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:42.040
We did it, Yoshika-chan.

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:42.840
Yeah!

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:47.470
<i>Thank you, Father.</i>

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:51.430
That light... Could that be the Neuroi's shattered pieces?

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:53.680
Yeah. Looks like they destroyed it.

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:55.520
Major! Are those two...

00:22:55.520 --> 00:22:58.180
Relax. They're both fine.

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:00.520
That unit...

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:04.070
The Magnificent Lightning? They completed it?

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:09.400
This is the new Fuso unit?

00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:12.740
J7W1, Magnificent Lightning.

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:15.200
I heard they ran into
a roadblock during its production,

00:23:15.200 --> 00:23:18.160
but due to Dr. Miyafuji's letter, they were able to complete it.

00:23:18.660 --> 00:23:20.000
The doctor's letter?

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:23.080
It's almost like it was
custom-built for her then.

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:24.960
So, what about our two battle heroes?

00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:27.510
They passed out as soon as they got back.

00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:30.380
They used up all the magic power they had.

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:31.300
It's understandable.

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.850
It's really amazing.

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:37.850
Miyafuji-san's magic power grew too powerful for her old Striker.

00:23:37.850 --> 00:23:39.940
It couldn't handle it.

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:45.440
Yeah. Seems there was a limiter installed, to prevent damage to the magic engine.

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:49.610
But the Magnificent Lightning should let her power reach its true potential.

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:52.610
She might not be a rookie anymore.

00:25:41.470 --> 00:25:45.690
Gallia, my homeland, still reels from the impact of the war.

00:25:45.690 --> 00:25:49.860
But my countrymen remain optimistic and still hold hope for tomorrow.

00:25:49.860 --> 00:25:54.070
Next time on <i>Strike Witches 2:</i> The Bridge to Tomorrow.
